1
00:00:09,309 --> 00:00:11,945
LIFE INSURANCE

2
00:00:23,323 --> 00:00:25,658
People have gone missing
on Mount Shikara, Hokkaido.

3
00:00:26,226 --> 00:00:28,161
One has died, and two have been rescued.

4
00:00:28,228 --> 00:00:30,230
Three remain missing.

5
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:32,899
Ms. Saruwatari. Open your eyes!

6
00:00:32,966 --> 00:00:34,034
Ms. Aya!

7
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:34,934
Thank you.

8
00:00:35,001 --> 00:00:36,436
You saved my life.

9
00:00:37,003 --> 00:00:40,373
According to Aya Saruwatari,
Ogoma's middle school teacher…

10
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,741
I'll go bring him back.

11
00:00:41,808 --> 00:00:43,243
No, I will.

12
00:00:43,977 --> 00:00:46,513
Everyone, please don't move for a while.

13
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:48,648
A heat pack.

14
00:00:49,315 --> 00:00:50,550
Thank you.

15
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,290
The deceased, Teruyuki Nikaido,
a restaurant owner,

16
00:00:57,357 --> 00:00:59,759
had his wife, Harune, as his beneficiary.

17
00:00:59,826 --> 00:01:03,897
She is now suspected
of insurance fraud for 150 million yen.

18
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:06,466
ORIENT DINER

19
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:13,740
Police! We're from Kitami HQ!

20
00:01:15,141 --> 00:01:15,975
I'm…

21
00:01:16,042 --> 00:01:17,610
I'm coming!

22
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:26,286
Hello, officers.

23
00:01:26,352 --> 00:01:27,220
Please, excuse us.

24
00:01:27,287 --> 00:01:30,390
May we borrow Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido's
computer and tablet?

25
00:01:30,957 --> 00:01:32,025
Of course.

26
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:36,262
73 HOURS HAVE PASSED

27
00:01:39,966 --> 00:01:41,601
Reinforcements from Kitami HQ.

28
00:01:42,402 --> 00:01:44,537
-Let's remain calm.
-Yes.

29
00:01:45,572 --> 00:01:46,906
Hello, sir. This way.

30
00:01:46,973 --> 00:01:47,874
Hello.

31
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:48,942
Hello.

32
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:53,079
Thank you all for your help
these past few days.

33
00:01:53,146 --> 00:01:54,747
Thank you, sir!

34
00:01:54,814 --> 00:01:57,450
Let's begin the investigation meeting.

35
00:01:57,517 --> 00:02:01,154
Three tour guests are still missing.
The search continues.

36
00:02:01,221 --> 00:02:04,124
Two people were rescued.
The guide, Motoka Tabatake,

37
00:02:04,190 --> 00:02:05,758
and the tour guest, Aya Saruwatari.

38
00:02:05,825 --> 00:02:10,296
Tabatake had moderate hypothermia
but regained consciousness earlier today.

39
00:02:10,363 --> 00:02:12,732
We've already questioned Saruwatari.

40
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:16,002
The body found was Teruyuki Nikaido, 44.

41
00:02:16,069 --> 00:02:18,071
The cause of death
was brain injury from a fall.

42
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:22,609
The autopsy found the sleeping pill
Zolpidem in his blood.

43
00:02:22,675 --> 00:02:26,546
He took it between 1:00 p.m. and 2:00 p.m.
on the day they went missing.

44
00:02:26,613 --> 00:02:28,548
He carried no medicine.

45
00:02:28,615 --> 00:02:31,818
We suspect someone made him
take it somehow.

46
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:33,786
Any possible motives?

47
00:02:33,853 --> 00:02:34,854
Yes!

48
00:02:35,388 --> 00:02:38,658
Nikaido had 150 million yen
in life insurance.

49
00:02:38,725 --> 00:02:42,095
It was 50 million at first,
but was increased two months ago.

50
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:44,264
The beneficiary is his wife, Harune.

51
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:48,201
Right after the body was found, she asked
the insurance company about the claim.

52
00:02:48,268 --> 00:02:50,270
She cared about money
more than her husband.

53
00:02:50,803 --> 00:02:52,305
One more point of suspicion.

54
00:02:52,872 --> 00:02:55,508
All the tour guests had hiking insurance.

55
00:02:55,575 --> 00:02:58,044
The beneficiary upon their death is…

56
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:00,146
Saruwatari.

57
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:02,182
Even for Nikaido?

58
00:03:02,248 --> 00:03:04,717
For all four, the three missing
and Nikaido.

59
00:03:04,784 --> 00:03:07,487
-20 million in total--
-I spoke to the insurance company!

60
00:03:08,154 --> 00:03:12,058
To receive the money, Saruwatari needs
the guests' consent and signatures.

61
00:03:12,125 --> 00:03:13,560
There are no signatures,

62
00:03:13,626 --> 00:03:16,629
so it's practically impossible
for her to get the 20 million yen.

63
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:19,866
Maybe she didn’t know and tried anyway.

64
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:23,169
The person who handled
the hiking insurance was Tabatake.

65
00:03:24,070 --> 00:03:24,904
Thank you.

66
00:03:25,738 --> 00:03:29,842
Guests can't see or change
other guests' applications.

67
00:03:30,810 --> 00:03:33,813
The only one who can is Tabatake.

68
00:03:37,650 --> 00:03:40,453
Does Tabatake or Saruwatari
have any connection to Nikaido’s wife?

69
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,488
We're checking their relationships.

70
00:03:42,555 --> 00:03:43,523
Yes.

71
00:03:45,024 --> 00:03:45,992
Hello.

72
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:46,893
Hello.

73
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:48,361
Did Ms. Saruwatari's surgery go well?

74
00:03:48,428 --> 00:03:50,029
It went well.

75
00:03:50,096 --> 00:03:51,331
Do you have time now?

76
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:52,632
Do I look like I do?

77
00:03:52,699 --> 00:03:54,367
I checked the hiking insurance.

78
00:03:54,434 --> 00:03:56,369
I checked too.

79
00:03:56,436 --> 00:03:57,537
Really?

80
00:03:58,137 --> 00:04:00,173
What’s with that smug look?

81
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:03,509
Ms. Saruwatari gets twenty million yen.

82
00:04:04,143 --> 00:04:05,011
Huh?

83
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:07,013
But she can't receive a single yen, right?

84
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,815
You looked into it.
As expected from the police.

85
00:04:08,881 --> 00:04:09,849
-Ogoma!
-Sorry.

86
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:11,417
Anyway, thanks for the information.

87
00:04:11,484 --> 00:04:12,785
I'll give you one more thing.

88
00:04:12,852 --> 00:04:13,953
You can tell me later.

89
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,555
-Hold up.
-What is it?

90
00:04:15,622 --> 00:04:17,657
Ms. Tabatake’s daughter, Nono…

91
00:04:18,358 --> 00:04:19,892
has a rare disease.

92
00:04:20,693 --> 00:04:21,761
Rare disease?

93
00:04:21,828 --> 00:04:22,662
Let's go!

94
00:04:23,529 --> 00:04:26,466
Coming! Please tell me more later.

95
00:04:27,533 --> 00:04:28,635
Sorry!

96
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:31,504
Sorry.

97
00:04:40,513 --> 00:04:42,215
Mommy is okay now.

98
00:04:43,016 --> 00:04:44,183
Don't worry.

99
00:04:44,250 --> 00:04:47,754
Please put on slippers
and use hand sanitizer.

100
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:48,688
Okay.

101
00:04:49,756 --> 00:04:50,823
I love you.

102
00:04:51,524 --> 00:04:52,458
I love you.

103
00:04:55,795 --> 00:04:57,096
Excuse me.

104
00:04:57,163 --> 00:04:58,398
Excuse me.

105
00:04:58,464 --> 00:05:00,333
I’m Awashima from the Shikara Station.

106
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:01,367
I’m Ogoma.

107
00:05:01,434 --> 00:05:03,936
Nono, go back to your room.

108
00:05:04,003 --> 00:05:04,937
Yes.

109
00:05:05,571 --> 00:05:07,507
Sorry, we'll make it quick.

110
00:05:09,075 --> 00:05:12,145
VISITOR PASS

111
00:05:13,046 --> 00:05:14,080
It's okay.

112
00:05:23,056 --> 00:05:24,490
Sorry to bother you.

113
00:05:24,557 --> 00:05:25,391
Hello.

114
00:05:25,458 --> 00:05:28,928
Can you tell us
what happened on the mountain?

115
00:05:29,929 --> 00:05:30,830
Yes.

116
00:05:33,099 --> 00:05:35,902
A tree fell when lightning struck, right?

117
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:39,505
I told everyone to stay there for a while.

118
00:05:40,473 --> 00:05:44,410
We'll wait here until the storm stops!

119
00:05:44,477 --> 00:05:47,914
But Mr. Nikaido went down alone.

120
00:05:49,682 --> 00:05:51,417
You tried to stop him, right?

121
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:53,586
Of course.

122
00:05:53,653 --> 00:05:57,056
But he wouldn't listen.

123
00:05:59,225 --> 00:06:02,495
While I was trying to deal with it,
Ms. Saruwatari said…

124
00:06:02,562 --> 00:06:04,030
I'll go bring him back.

125
00:06:04,097 --> 00:06:05,131
What?

126
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:07,233
I'll convince him to come back.

127
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:08,167
A heat pack.

128
00:06:12,271 --> 00:06:13,139
What?

129
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,476
Ms. Saruwatari?

130
00:06:17,777 --> 00:06:19,779
-She went after him?
-Yes.

131
00:06:22,615 --> 00:06:25,818
As the guide,
I should've convinced him to stay.

132
00:06:26,386 --> 00:06:30,156
But I couldn't leave the other guests.

133
00:06:30,790 --> 00:06:32,024
It's my fault.

134
00:06:32,792 --> 00:06:34,327
I'm sorry.

135
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:37,663
Who prepared the food and drinks?

136
00:06:38,231 --> 00:06:41,267
Each guest prepared their own.

137
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:46,272
I told them in advance to bring meals,
snacks, and water.

138
00:06:46,339 --> 00:06:48,107
Even the late Mr. Nikaido?

139
00:06:48,674 --> 00:06:51,778
Mr. Nikaido was basically empty-handed.

140
00:06:51,844 --> 00:06:55,882
Did he eat or drink anything
during the climb?

141
00:06:57,984 --> 00:07:00,887
I saw Ms. Saruwatari give him water.

142
00:07:02,522 --> 00:07:06,626
She gave him her own?

143
00:07:06,692 --> 00:07:07,760
Yes.

144
00:07:08,694 --> 00:07:10,363
Ms. Saruwatari

145
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:14,267
kept worrying about him
because he was unprepared.

146
00:07:15,201 --> 00:07:17,036
More than worried,

147
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:21,908
she looked angry at him
for climbing in light clothes.

148
00:07:21,974 --> 00:07:25,278
This pink flower
is the pixie-eye primrose.

149
00:07:26,112 --> 00:07:29,382
-It has five petals--
-Please don't go ahead of the guide.

150
00:07:33,052 --> 00:07:34,487
Mr. Nikaido.

151
00:07:35,822 --> 00:07:37,990
Isn't there any place to get water?

152
00:07:38,057 --> 00:07:39,325
No.

153
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:41,861
You again?

154
00:07:45,932 --> 00:07:48,701
Drinking it all before going down…

155
00:07:48,768 --> 00:07:50,303
I don't understand you.

156
00:07:51,237 --> 00:07:52,939
So you're not all bad.

157
00:07:57,243 --> 00:07:59,111
What time was that?

158
00:08:00,112 --> 00:08:03,115
During the descent.
Before the lightning started.

159
00:08:05,651 --> 00:08:06,719
Around 1:00 p.m.

160
00:08:08,254 --> 00:08:09,288
Excuse me.

161
00:08:10,223 --> 00:08:14,760
Did anyone besides Ms. Saruwatari
give him food or drink?

162
00:08:15,428 --> 00:08:16,462
No.

163
00:08:16,529 --> 00:08:18,264
Can I ask one more question?

164
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:22,635
Before the tour, all five guests
got hiking insurance.

165
00:08:22,702 --> 00:08:25,872
Do you know who the beneficiary is?

166
00:08:26,806 --> 00:08:28,341
Their families, right?

167
00:08:28,875 --> 00:08:32,044
All five had a third party
as a beneficiary.

168
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:36,616
Who is it?

169
00:08:36,682 --> 00:08:38,284
Aya Saruwatari.

170
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:39,485
Were you aware of this?

171
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:43,589
I had no idea. That's impossible.

172
00:08:45,157 --> 00:08:46,425
Could you have

173
00:08:47,693 --> 00:08:49,595
made a mistake on the tablet?

174
00:08:50,897 --> 00:08:53,266
A mistake like that
would be a huge problem.

175
00:08:55,434 --> 00:08:56,569
Detective…

176
00:09:00,273 --> 00:09:03,609
I'm the beneficiary? Why is my name there?

177
00:09:03,676 --> 00:09:07,046
We heard you were worried
about Mr. Nikaido during the climb.

178
00:09:08,014 --> 00:09:09,048
Yes.

179
00:09:09,115 --> 00:09:10,850
Why was that?

180
00:09:10,917 --> 00:09:12,251
Why, you ask?

181
00:09:13,052 --> 00:09:19,125
He didn't appear used to climbing,
so I spoke to him a few times.

182
00:09:19,959 --> 00:09:21,561
Did you argue?

183
00:09:23,262 --> 00:09:24,964
No, it wasn't that serious.

184
00:09:27,199 --> 00:09:30,236
Did Mr. Nikaido run out of water
on the way down?

185
00:09:30,803 --> 00:09:31,871
Yes.

186
00:09:32,505 --> 00:09:35,074
Who gave him water at that time?

187
00:09:36,042 --> 00:09:37,476
Ms. Tabatake.

188
00:09:38,311 --> 00:09:40,580
Not you? Ms. Tabatake?

189
00:09:40,646 --> 00:09:41,647
Yes.

190
00:09:53,659 --> 00:09:56,228
What are you investigating?

191
00:09:56,295 --> 00:09:58,664
We're just checking what happened.

192
00:10:00,533 --> 00:10:02,301
They're each saying different things.

193
00:10:02,368 --> 00:10:04,670
One of them is lying.

194
00:10:04,737 --> 00:10:07,707
Their statements don't match.
Tell the station right away.

195
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:08,774
Got it.

196
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,381
Are you done interviewing?

197
00:10:16,182 --> 00:10:17,083
Yes.

198
00:10:17,149 --> 00:10:19,552
Then can I get their statements too?

199
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:22,755
I need the accident details for my report.

200
00:10:22,822 --> 00:10:25,191
Did you forget the Hakodate case?

201
00:10:27,393 --> 00:10:30,296
That fake family suicide case.

202
00:10:30,363 --> 00:10:31,998
I handled it.

203
00:10:32,832 --> 00:10:34,166
What a surprise.

204
00:10:34,233 --> 00:10:36,602
How did you know it was murder?

205
00:10:38,671 --> 00:10:40,806
Maybe we're just looking at it
from different angles.

206
00:10:40,873 --> 00:10:43,175
The police care about motive and evidence.

207
00:10:43,242 --> 00:10:46,412
I follow money. Only money.

208
00:10:46,479 --> 00:10:49,815
Your tip made the police lose face.

209
00:10:52,118 --> 00:10:54,020
Would you rather I hadn't reported them?

210
00:10:54,754 --> 00:10:57,089
The mistress
who killed a family of four in a fire?

211
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:59,191
-Should I not have--
-Are you picking a fight?

212
00:10:59,258 --> 00:11:02,828
If anything, you're picking one with me.

213
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:04,730
Did it hurt your career?

214
00:11:04,797 --> 00:11:07,833
I'm now stationed in the middle
of nowhere. Take the hint.

215
00:11:08,734 --> 00:11:10,970
Sorry, I'm bad at hints.

216
00:11:11,037 --> 00:11:13,339
-If you have tips, give them to us early.
-Got it!

217
00:11:18,044 --> 00:11:20,646
Thank you very much for saving me.

218
00:11:20,713 --> 00:11:23,849
It was nothing. It was Ogoma
who found you. Excuse me.

219
00:11:23,916 --> 00:11:24,817
Okay.

220
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:30,723
Are you looking into Mr. Nikaido?

221
00:11:32,925 --> 00:11:37,430
Is there something suspicious
about his death?

222
00:11:37,496 --> 00:11:41,600
I'm investigating, and so are the police.

223
00:11:43,069 --> 00:11:45,271
Let's talk casually.

224
00:11:46,172 --> 00:11:47,840
Where should I start?

225
00:11:48,908 --> 00:11:51,110
What's your relationship with Ogoma?

226
00:11:51,177 --> 00:11:52,978
Hello.

227
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:55,548
The critical 72 hours have passed.

228
00:11:55,614 --> 00:11:57,083
What about the missing people?

229
00:11:57,149 --> 00:11:59,752
Ryutaro Monden, 30, office worker.

230
00:11:59,819 --> 00:12:02,688
His wife, Misaki, 31, housewife.

231
00:12:02,755 --> 00:12:04,690
Hitoshi Uematsu, 52, civil servant.

232
00:12:04,757 --> 00:12:06,692
-We already know that.
-Their addresses?

233
00:12:06,759 --> 00:12:09,495
We don't disclose addresses
or job details.

234
00:12:11,263 --> 00:12:14,800
Base to all teams! If you find anything
the missing people may have left,

235
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:18,804
including trash like plastic bottles,
collect it right away!

236
00:12:18,871 --> 00:12:22,341
After that, ask the local station
to help sort it,

237
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:24,543
and send it to forensics!

238
00:12:24,610 --> 00:12:26,545
This is getting serious.

239
00:12:26,612 --> 00:12:28,948
What happened in those mountains?

240
00:12:29,014 --> 00:12:32,618
The three missing people
weren't drugged too, were they?

241
00:12:32,685 --> 00:12:34,553
I hope not.

242
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:37,389
Everyone, keep working while you listen.

243
00:12:37,456 --> 00:12:40,693
Tomorrow, support will come
from Kitami HQ.

244
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:43,863
They'll handle the interviews.

245
00:12:43,929 --> 00:12:45,898
We'll move on to canvassing the area.

246
00:12:45,965 --> 00:12:48,267
-Huh?
-Mr. Awashima and Ogoma.

247
00:12:48,334 --> 00:12:51,003
Look into Mr. Nikaido's friends
and security footage.

248
00:12:51,070 --> 00:12:53,939
Also, check the security cameras
near his home.

249
00:12:54,006 --> 00:12:55,107
That's not fair!

250
00:12:55,841 --> 00:12:58,878
Let Mr. Awashima and me
keep interviewing people.

251
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:00,212
We are local officers!

252
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:02,982
Interviews depend on experience.

253
00:13:03,048 --> 00:13:04,517
It's like pros and amateurs.

254
00:13:04,583 --> 00:13:06,218
-I have some experience too!
-Ogoma.

255
00:13:09,522 --> 00:13:11,190
I'm 30 already.

256
00:13:12,858 --> 00:13:15,127
That's half my age, you know.

257
00:13:15,194 --> 00:13:17,163
How did your investigation go?

258
00:13:17,229 --> 00:13:19,565
What do the police think?
Is it an accident? Murder?

259
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:22,835
Their investigation is just starting!

260
00:13:25,271 --> 00:13:31,977
Even if it's murder by sleeping pill,
it's very unlikely Harune did it herself.

261
00:13:32,611 --> 00:13:35,815
It will take time to find out
if she was even involved.

262
00:13:35,881 --> 00:13:39,351
"I see! It takes time!"
Did you think I'd say that?!

263
00:13:39,418 --> 00:13:42,621
Hurry and find Harune Nikaido
and the people around her,

264
00:13:42,688 --> 00:13:44,290
and get the report in!

265
00:13:44,356 --> 00:13:45,558
Got it.

266
00:13:50,396 --> 00:13:52,064
Where do I go now?

267
00:14:03,809 --> 00:14:05,244
The funeral is tomorrow.

268
00:14:05,311 --> 00:14:08,914
We don't have much time,
and I don't know where to start.

269
00:14:08,981 --> 00:14:10,549
Can you help?

270
00:14:10,616 --> 00:14:13,886
Also, how is that thing I asked you to do?

271
00:14:16,021 --> 00:14:16,989
Okay.

272
00:14:17,957 --> 00:14:19,058
Excuse me.

273
00:14:19,124 --> 00:14:19,959
Yes?

274
00:14:20,025 --> 00:14:21,260
Can I try this on?

275
00:14:21,327 --> 00:14:23,229
This way, please.

276
00:14:26,899 --> 00:14:27,600
Huh?

277
00:14:29,235 --> 00:14:31,637
Oh, my! What a coincidence!

278
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:38,611
I'm sorry I asked you a ton
of rude questions the other day.

279
00:14:40,012 --> 00:14:41,347
May I sit here?

280
00:14:41,413 --> 00:14:44,016
Of course not.
I don't want to see your face.

281
00:14:44,083 --> 00:14:45,117
Excuse me.

282
00:14:47,219 --> 00:14:50,089
About the contract change two months ago--

283
00:14:50,155 --> 00:14:51,390
I don’t know.

284
00:14:52,658 --> 00:14:54,994
It was increased
to 150 million yen, because…

285
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:56,462
I don’t know.

286
00:14:58,430 --> 00:14:59,365
Well, let's eat.

287
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:02,601
Delicious.

288
00:15:02,668 --> 00:15:04,937
CART STORAGE

289
00:15:50,749 --> 00:15:54,186
I'll be talking to your friends
and acquaintances, then.

290
00:15:56,922 --> 00:15:58,857
Three people are still missing.

291
00:15:58,924 --> 00:16:03,963
We're stopping for today,
but it has already been over 76 hours.

292
00:16:04,029 --> 00:16:07,199
Let's use all our strength
to find them as soon as possible.

293
00:16:07,266 --> 00:16:08,901
That's all from base.

294
00:16:24,016 --> 00:16:25,551
Ogoma speaking.

295
00:16:25,617 --> 00:16:26,986
Can we talk now?

296
00:16:36,362 --> 00:16:37,830
Of course.

297
00:16:39,398 --> 00:16:42,334
Sorry for interviewing you
right after your surgery.

298
00:16:44,303 --> 00:16:48,340
Did you misremember something?
Mix some details up?

299
00:16:51,477 --> 00:16:53,045
Of course.

300
00:16:54,279 --> 00:16:57,282
Nikaido's death is an accident, right?

301
00:16:58,951 --> 00:17:00,719
We're still investigating that.

302
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:03,122
Was he poisoned?

303
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:07,659
No poison, no.

304
00:17:08,927 --> 00:17:12,064
Am I a suspect now?

305
00:17:13,899 --> 00:17:15,534
Not at all.

306
00:17:20,806 --> 00:17:25,544
We may ask for your help again,
but don't worry.

307
00:17:29,148 --> 00:17:31,750
Do you need anything?

308
00:17:34,686 --> 00:17:35,954
A nail clipper.

309
00:17:36,955 --> 00:17:38,157
Huh?

310
00:17:40,359 --> 00:17:43,929
If you bring me one, it would help a lot.

311
00:17:43,996 --> 00:17:46,065
Okay. I'll bring one.

312
00:17:46,131 --> 00:17:47,132
Okay.

313
00:17:47,766 --> 00:17:49,501
Anytime is fine.

314
00:17:50,702 --> 00:17:51,770
See you.

315
00:17:52,638 --> 00:17:53,539
Bye.

316
00:17:55,741 --> 00:17:59,611
OGOMA

317
00:17:59,678 --> 00:18:00,879
Just ring the bell once.

318
00:18:00,946 --> 00:18:02,347
-Lend me your washing machine.
-No.

319
00:18:02,414 --> 00:18:04,416
-Hey!
-What?

320
00:18:04,483 --> 00:18:06,285
The coin laundry went under, right?

321
00:18:06,351 --> 00:18:08,754
Yeah. It went bankrupt before I came here.

322
00:18:08,821 --> 00:18:12,224
If you know that,
lend me your washing machine!

323
00:18:12,291 --> 00:18:14,026
Wash it in the bath!

324
00:18:14,526 --> 00:18:15,427
Please.

325
00:18:15,494 --> 00:18:16,595
Today.

326
00:18:16,662 --> 00:18:19,364
Just for today. Please.

327
00:18:24,970 --> 00:18:28,073
Drink as much as you like. I don’t drink.

328
00:18:28,140 --> 00:18:30,742
I planned to finish investigating
in two or three days,

329
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:34,146
but it looks like it will drag on.

330
00:18:35,380 --> 00:18:36,548
Thanks.

331
00:18:38,317 --> 00:18:40,919
Can you tell me your info then?

332
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:45,023
Why are you suddenly
acting like a detective? What info?

333
00:18:45,090 --> 00:18:48,293
About Ms. Tabatake's daughter.
She has a rare disease, right?

334
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:52,064
Yes. The name is ECO deficiency.

335
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:54,299
It's a rare immune disease
caused by a gene mutation.

336
00:18:54,867 --> 00:18:57,769
Her immune system,
which should protect the body,

337
00:18:57,836 --> 00:19:00,105
went haywire and now attacks
the body's own cells.

338
00:19:00,639 --> 00:19:03,442
I see. What are the symptoms?

339
00:19:03,509 --> 00:19:06,712
In the active phase, the lymph nodes
and liver become severely swollen.

340
00:19:07,379 --> 00:19:09,381
Normally, her fevers
take longer to go down,

341
00:19:09,448 --> 00:19:11,383
and bleeding doesn’t stop easily.

342
00:19:11,450 --> 00:19:14,786
Well, if it gets worse, it can be fatal.

343
00:19:15,687 --> 00:19:17,489
Is she in serious condition?

344
00:19:18,857 --> 00:19:21,560
She seems fairly stable now.

345
00:19:21,627 --> 00:19:25,497
She's had a low fever for a while,
so she's in the hospital, just to be safe.

346
00:19:26,598 --> 00:19:28,567
How can it be cured?

347
00:19:29,134 --> 00:19:31,103
It can't be cured easily. It's chronic.

348
00:19:32,604 --> 00:19:37,876
Gene therapy might remove the cause,
and she can be cured that way.

349
00:19:38,577 --> 00:19:42,881
But they can't try it
until she's more stable.

350
00:19:44,149 --> 00:19:47,386
For now, medicine to control the symptoms
is the best they can do.

351
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:51,657
Does the treatment cost a lot?

352
00:19:51,723 --> 00:19:53,725
You smell money too, don't you?

353
00:19:54,626 --> 00:19:57,329
But this disease gets government support.

354
00:19:57,396 --> 00:20:00,165
The cost isn't high enough
to ruin your life.

355
00:20:00,232 --> 00:20:02,768
You talk about money a lot.

356
00:20:03,468 --> 00:20:06,772
Nothing shows
a person's nature like money.

357
00:20:07,439 --> 00:20:10,209
Without even meeting someone,
once I see their bank records,

358
00:20:10,275 --> 00:20:12,678
I can understand everything about them.

359
00:20:13,245 --> 00:20:15,681
If that were true, we police officers
wouldn't struggle.

360
00:20:15,747 --> 00:20:17,149
Show me your bankbook then.

361
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,083
Hey.

362
00:20:18,817 --> 00:20:21,520
Ms. Tabatake is a single mother.

363
00:20:21,587 --> 00:20:24,856
That's prejudice against single parents.

364
00:20:24,923 --> 00:20:27,960
-That's prejudice!
-Do you think single mothers are all poor?

365
00:20:28,026 --> 00:20:31,230
-She's doing her best for Nono.
-She even works as a driver on the side.

366
00:20:31,296 --> 00:20:32,431
Ms. Tabatake…

367
00:20:32,497 --> 00:20:35,100
She and Nono are doing their best.

368
00:20:35,167 --> 00:20:36,268
Sorry.

369
00:20:39,171 --> 00:20:40,072
Go ahead.

370
00:20:41,873 --> 00:20:43,976
I talked to the coroner
who autopsied the body.

371
00:20:44,042 --> 00:20:45,110
You're fast.

372
00:20:47,312 --> 00:20:50,115
Who do the police think
gave the sleeping pills,

373
00:20:50,182 --> 00:20:52,551
Ms. Tabatake or Ms. Saruwatari?

374
00:20:53,118 --> 00:20:54,553
We're still investigating.

375
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:58,557
Who do you think did it, Ogoma?

376
00:20:59,124 --> 00:21:00,692
You tell me first.

377
00:21:00,759 --> 00:21:03,595
No. You tell me first.

378
00:21:03,662 --> 00:21:05,063
No. Here you go.

379
00:21:05,130 --> 00:21:06,164
Thanks.

380
00:21:06,832 --> 00:21:08,333
Okay. At the same time.

381
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:09,534
-Ms. Aya!
-Ms. Tabatake!

382
00:21:09,601 --> 00:21:11,470
Why Ms. Aya?

383
00:21:11,536 --> 00:21:12,704
By elimination.

384
00:21:12,771 --> 00:21:13,705
What?

385
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:17,009
Ms. Tabatake earns money
for her child's sake.

386
00:21:17,075 --> 00:21:20,779
Would a parent
commit insurance murder for that?

387
00:21:20,846 --> 00:21:22,547
I thought about it.

388
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:24,850
-What?
-You actually think?

389
00:21:26,652 --> 00:21:30,522
Could Harune have given it to him
when he left home?

390
00:21:30,589 --> 00:21:33,659
Maybe she gave him
a slow-dissolving capsule or…

391
00:21:33,725 --> 00:21:35,927
I've handled cases like that.

392
00:21:36,895 --> 00:21:37,996
There's a delay, right?

393
00:21:38,664 --> 00:21:41,466
But the delay is only one or two hours.

394
00:21:41,533 --> 00:21:43,702
It wouldn't take until the descent.

395
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:47,105
Then it needs an accomplice.

396
00:21:47,172 --> 00:21:52,010
Either Ms. Tabatake
or Ms. Aya is the accomplice.

397
00:21:52,611 --> 00:21:54,346
The one who carried out the crime.

398
00:21:59,217 --> 00:22:01,853
I'm going to see Harune tomorrow.

399
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:04,389
That woman never answers the phone.

400
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:08,627
Your face… Are you coming with me?

401
00:22:10,562 --> 00:22:11,563
No.

402
00:22:12,230 --> 00:22:14,499
-I'm not doing the interrogating.
-Why?

403
00:22:14,566 --> 00:22:16,601
I'm not free like you.

404
00:22:18,570 --> 00:22:21,340
Tomorrow, please tell me
what Harune tells you.

405
00:22:21,406 --> 00:22:22,741
Huh…

406
00:22:22,808 --> 00:22:25,677
In exchange, tell me
some investigation info.

407
00:22:25,744 --> 00:22:28,146
-No.
-There you go again.

408
00:22:28,213 --> 00:22:30,682
I hate that about the police.

409
00:22:30,749 --> 00:22:34,252
They dig into everything about you,
but give nothing back.

410
00:22:34,319 --> 00:22:35,754
I lent you my washing machine!

411
00:22:35,821 --> 00:22:37,389
I bought you beer!

412
00:22:37,456 --> 00:22:39,157
I haven't drunk it!

413
00:22:41,793 --> 00:22:42,828
Rain?

414
00:22:44,963 --> 00:22:48,567
The police stopped the search today
because of heavy rain.

415
00:22:48,633 --> 00:22:49,568
Here's your meal.

416
00:22:49,634 --> 00:22:52,738
-They will resume when weather improves.
-Your name, please.

417
00:22:52,804 --> 00:22:55,640
-Aya Saruwatari. Thank you.
-Enjoy.

418
00:22:55,707 --> 00:22:59,644
Two men and one woman are still missing.

419
00:23:00,345 --> 00:23:03,248
In this accident,
there has been one casualty…

420
00:23:03,315 --> 00:23:05,884
Ms. Saruwatari, you have a visitor.

421
00:23:05,951 --> 00:23:07,119
Now?

422
00:23:07,819 --> 00:23:12,224
We're collecting fingerprints
from everyone involved.

423
00:23:12,891 --> 00:23:14,726
-Fingerprints?
-Yes.

424
00:23:14,793 --> 00:23:17,396
It's voluntary, but will you help?

425
00:23:19,731 --> 00:23:21,266
Your hair is so messy.

426
00:23:23,969 --> 00:23:26,037
All right. Huh?

427
00:23:26,104 --> 00:23:28,073
You have terrible bed hair.

428
00:23:28,774 --> 00:23:30,742
I want another hair tie.

429
00:23:30,809 --> 00:23:32,043
Hair tie?

430
00:23:32,878 --> 00:23:35,180
Okay. Here.

431
00:23:38,283 --> 00:23:42,020
Dr. Yoshino said I could
maybe leave the hospital with you.

432
00:23:44,456 --> 00:23:46,124
I hope you can.

433
00:23:46,191 --> 00:23:48,260
Excuse me. We're from Kitami HQ.

434
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:52,030
We're here to ask
about what happened on the 27th.

435
00:23:53,698 --> 00:23:55,534
Give me a moment.

436
00:24:04,209 --> 00:24:06,478
Were you acquainted with Mr. Nikaido?

437
00:24:06,545 --> 00:24:08,180
No.

438
00:24:08,246 --> 00:24:10,348
He looked kind of, you know…

439
00:24:10,415 --> 00:24:11,550
Kind of what?

440
00:24:12,217 --> 00:24:14,252
He looked shady, so I couldn't trust him.

441
00:24:37,142 --> 00:24:39,044
Hello?

442
00:24:45,450 --> 00:24:48,053
Is anyone here?

443
00:24:51,523 --> 00:24:53,492
Hello?

444
00:24:54,526 --> 00:24:58,196
Hey! What?! I'm scared!

445
00:25:10,308 --> 00:25:12,611
-What's wrong?
-It's just…

446
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:14,012
This car…

447
00:25:18,984 --> 00:25:20,218
Let's go!

448
00:25:20,285 --> 00:25:21,119
Okay!

449
00:25:29,628 --> 00:25:31,296
-No one is here?
-Yeah.

450
00:25:31,363 --> 00:25:32,564
Let's go.

451
00:25:33,398 --> 00:25:36,334
-Shut up!
-What are you doing! No! Stop!

452
00:25:36,401 --> 00:25:39,204
Shut up!

453
00:25:39,771 --> 00:25:40,605
Is it here?

454
00:25:40,672 --> 00:25:41,840
Should be.

455
00:25:41,907 --> 00:25:43,375
-Do you need anything?
-Yeah.

456
00:25:43,441 --> 00:25:44,576
We're with the police.

457
00:25:45,176 --> 00:25:47,979
Does anyone here work
at the restaurant, Orient Diner?

458
00:25:48,046 --> 00:25:49,614
Do you have an ID?

459
00:25:49,681 --> 00:25:50,615
You do?

460
00:25:50,682 --> 00:25:51,783
You do?

461
00:25:51,850 --> 00:25:54,319
-I'm Awashima from the local station.
-Ogoma.

462
00:25:56,221 --> 00:26:00,959
We want to ask about the owner,
Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido.

463
00:26:03,261 --> 00:26:04,796
What will happen to the diner?

464
00:26:04,863 --> 00:26:07,399
Did he act strange recently?

465
00:26:07,465 --> 00:26:08,600
No.

466
00:26:08,667 --> 00:26:09,968
-No.
-Not at all?

467
00:26:10,035 --> 00:26:11,236
He didn't act strange at all?

468
00:26:12,070 --> 00:26:13,204
Does he hike often?

469
00:26:13,271 --> 00:26:14,205
He does.

470
00:26:14,906 --> 00:26:16,975
He often calls
to say he's going on a hike.

471
00:26:17,042 --> 00:26:18,310
Who does he call?

472
00:26:18,376 --> 00:26:19,511
His wife?

473
00:26:19,578 --> 00:26:20,579
His wife?

474
00:26:21,246 --> 00:26:22,314
Or a friend?

475
00:26:23,515 --> 00:26:24,649
A friend?

476
00:26:27,953 --> 00:26:29,521
Oh, Liam!

477
00:26:30,522 --> 00:26:31,890
-Are they diner staff?
-Yes.

478
00:26:31,957 --> 00:26:33,658
I'm good.

479
00:26:33,725 --> 00:26:35,093
It's the police.

480
00:26:35,794 --> 00:26:37,262
Hey! Wait!

481
00:26:37,329 --> 00:26:40,265
Wait! Stop!

482
00:26:40,332 --> 00:26:42,067
Hey! I said stop!

483
00:26:42,133 --> 00:26:44,069
Can we talk?

484
00:26:51,109 --> 00:26:52,177
Open the car.

485
00:26:53,945 --> 00:26:54,813
Excuse me.

486
00:26:57,115 --> 00:26:58,416
I'm going to open it.

487
00:27:00,552 --> 00:27:02,621
Calm down!

488
00:27:02,687 --> 00:27:04,222
Let's get you down.

489
00:27:06,391 --> 00:27:08,460
Okay. Ouch, that hurt!

490
00:27:08,526 --> 00:27:11,129
It hurts! Calm down!

491
00:27:11,196 --> 00:27:12,998
I'm with the police! It's okay!

492
00:27:13,064 --> 00:27:14,366
I'm with the police!

493
00:27:18,169 --> 00:27:19,771
It's you?

494
00:27:20,572 --> 00:27:22,240
-Okay.
-I love the police!

495
00:27:23,141 --> 00:27:26,211
Okay, you're pretty strong.
Let me go already.

496
00:27:31,583 --> 00:27:33,118
-Boss.
-What?

497
00:27:33,184 --> 00:27:34,953
So it wasn't a kidnapping?

498
00:27:35,020 --> 00:27:36,087
No.

499
00:27:36,855 --> 00:27:39,157
I asked them earlier.

500
00:27:39,724 --> 00:27:43,128
They said Nao broke into their shop.

501
00:27:43,194 --> 00:27:45,797
So they caught him
to hand him to the police.

502
00:27:45,864 --> 00:27:46,698
Sorry.

503
00:27:46,765 --> 00:27:50,235
But one of them
had an expired residence card.

504
00:27:50,301 --> 00:27:51,703
He was staying illegally.

505
00:27:57,008 --> 00:27:58,543
Please say that in Japanese.

506
00:27:59,744 --> 00:28:01,146
Is the interpreter here yet?

507
00:28:01,212 --> 00:28:03,415
Hey. Wipe your sweat.

508
00:28:04,883 --> 00:28:06,584
You're making a mess.

509
00:28:10,021 --> 00:28:11,456
It's open.

510
00:28:11,523 --> 00:28:13,558
I hope we can go home soon.

511
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:16,494
I'm fine with staying here forever.

512
00:28:17,162 --> 00:28:18,329
Why?

513
00:28:18,396 --> 00:28:20,999
I can be with you more in the hospital.

514
00:28:24,002 --> 00:28:26,871
When we leave the hospital,
let's binge-watch Dandadan.

515
00:28:27,806 --> 00:28:28,940
And order pizza.

516
00:28:29,574 --> 00:28:32,610
Will we get the one with crab?
I like that one.

517
00:28:33,445 --> 00:28:34,913
I like it too.

518
00:28:36,381 --> 00:28:37,582
What are you looking at?

519
00:28:41,319 --> 00:28:42,420
Officer.

520
00:28:43,021 --> 00:28:44,122
Yes?

521
00:28:44,189 --> 00:28:47,292
Would you like some pudding too?

522
00:28:47,358 --> 00:28:48,493
No, it's for your daughter.

523
00:28:50,061 --> 00:28:52,997
You can't eat two, right?
Let's give him one.

524
00:28:54,132 --> 00:28:55,667
I don't know…

525
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:57,135
Your call.

526
00:28:57,702 --> 00:28:58,803
Let's give him one.

527
00:28:58,870 --> 00:29:01,172
Are you sure?
Then can you bring this to him?

528
00:29:02,307 --> 00:29:03,274
May I?

529
00:29:04,275 --> 00:29:06,811
I'll take it, okay? Thank you.

530
00:29:12,650 --> 00:29:13,885
Ms. Aya.

531
00:29:28,933 --> 00:29:30,835
-Yes?
-We found fingerprints.

532
00:29:30,902 --> 00:29:34,439
From the bottle collected on the mountain,
we found Nikaido's saliva

533
00:29:35,373 --> 00:29:37,142
and Saruwatari's fingerprints.

534
00:29:37,642 --> 00:29:40,912
Sleeping pill residue
was also found inside the bottle.

535
00:29:40,979 --> 00:29:43,414
HQ is stepping in!

536
00:29:44,883 --> 00:29:45,950
Um…

537
00:29:47,685 --> 00:29:49,621
What about Ms. Tabatake's fingerprints?

538
00:29:50,922 --> 00:29:52,624
We didn't find any.

539
00:29:55,426 --> 00:29:58,596
It's now clear whose statement was right.

540
00:29:59,330 --> 00:30:03,668
Tomorrow morning,
we'll question Saruwatari in detail.

541
00:30:05,036 --> 00:30:08,173
Am I a suspect now?

542
00:30:13,845 --> 00:30:15,446
You are.

543
00:30:24,689 --> 00:30:27,425
I saw Ms. Saruwatari give him water.

544
00:30:27,492 --> 00:30:30,395
Could you have
made a mistake on the tablet?

545
00:30:30,461 --> 00:30:32,964
A mistake like that
would be a huge problem.

546
00:30:40,171 --> 00:30:41,306
Laundry machine again?

547
00:30:41,372 --> 00:30:44,809
Thank you for saving my life today.

548
00:30:44,876 --> 00:30:45,844
Sure.

549
00:30:45,910 --> 00:30:48,913
-Know any places to drink around here?
-Everything closes at 9:00 p.m. here.

550
00:30:49,814 --> 00:30:53,351
I want to show my thanks.

551
00:30:53,418 --> 00:30:54,586
Let me treat you.

552
00:30:54,652 --> 00:30:56,120
No need.

553
00:30:56,187 --> 00:30:58,957
Ogoma! You'll crush my head!

554
00:31:02,060 --> 00:31:04,362
I thought I would be killed.

555
00:31:04,929 --> 00:31:08,366
In that situation,
I didn't care about money anymore.

556
00:31:08,433 --> 00:31:10,869
I would have paid
everything I own to be saved.

557
00:31:10,935 --> 00:31:13,404
They didn't seem to want to kill you.

558
00:31:14,138 --> 00:31:16,274
They wanted to hand you
over to the police.

559
00:31:17,508 --> 00:31:18,977
Did you do something wrong?

560
00:31:21,479 --> 00:31:23,615
I did nothing. Here.

561
00:31:25,250 --> 00:31:26,284
Thanks.

562
00:31:27,018 --> 00:31:29,087
Did you find out anything after that?

563
00:31:33,291 --> 00:31:35,860
I may have been wrong.

564
00:31:40,565 --> 00:31:43,768
About who gave
Mr. Nikaido the sleeping pill.

565
00:31:45,904 --> 00:31:49,240
Was it Ms. Aya?

566
00:31:51,542 --> 00:31:52,644
We found fingerprints.

567
00:31:53,378 --> 00:31:56,114
What is Ms. Aya to you, Ogoma?

568
00:31:56,781 --> 00:31:57,682
Your first love?

569
00:31:57,749 --> 00:31:58,683
It’s not like that.

570
00:31:58,750 --> 00:32:00,351
-She saved me…
-She is pretty.

571
00:32:00,418 --> 00:32:01,452
I'm grateful to her!

572
00:32:01,519 --> 00:32:03,254
I hear she's single.

573
00:32:03,321 --> 00:32:04,822
I'm just grateful to her!

574
00:32:04,889 --> 00:32:06,090
Ow!

575
00:32:06,791 --> 00:32:07,892
Okay, I get it.

576
00:32:09,360 --> 00:32:12,030
Since we're here, tell me about Ms. Aya.

577
00:32:35,553 --> 00:32:36,721
Hello?

578
00:33:05,316 --> 00:33:06,451
Nono.

579
00:33:09,454 --> 00:33:10,455
Nono.

580
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:14,826
Mommy?

581
00:33:21,899 --> 00:33:23,034
I'm sorry.

582
00:33:26,771 --> 00:33:30,274
I'm sorry. I have to go home for a bit.

583
00:33:32,577 --> 00:33:35,980
The town I grew up in was dangerous.

584
00:33:36,047 --> 00:33:37,115
Where?

585
00:33:37,181 --> 00:33:38,116
Koura Town.

586
00:33:38,850 --> 00:33:40,018
Right.

587
00:33:40,084 --> 00:33:42,553
That town has assault cases every day.

588
00:33:42,620 --> 00:33:45,056
Everyone's parents
were either ex-convicts,

589
00:33:45,123 --> 00:33:47,058
in prison, or addicts.

590
00:33:47,125 --> 00:33:48,926
Are you sure you grew up in Japan?

591
00:33:48,993 --> 00:33:50,328
-Anything you can't eat?
-What?

592
00:33:50,395 --> 00:33:51,763
What foods do you hate?

593
00:33:52,463 --> 00:33:54,532
Like bamboo shoots?

594
00:33:54,599 --> 00:33:56,434
Give me some. Here.

595
00:33:56,501 --> 00:33:58,503
Our parents didn't keep a close eye on us.

596
00:33:58,569 --> 00:34:02,473
So some of us did terrible things,
like assault, theft,

597
00:34:03,341 --> 00:34:06,277
or selling things washed up
on the shore to the yakuza.

598
00:34:06,344 --> 00:34:07,879
-You mean seaweed?
-No.

599
00:34:08,546 --> 00:34:11,616
Drugs thrown from smuggling ships.

600
00:34:11,682 --> 00:34:15,520
When the coast guard chased them,
they threw the cargo into the sea.

601
00:34:16,687 --> 00:34:20,558
I saw some addicts naked, going wild,

602
00:34:20,625 --> 00:34:22,860
so I knew those drugs were bad.

603
00:34:24,429 --> 00:34:27,231
But in middle school,
you want to try risky stuff, right?

604
00:34:27,832 --> 00:34:30,168
I only cared about entrance exams.

605
00:34:30,868 --> 00:34:31,869
Well,

606
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:37,508
an older friend of mine
said he found drugs at the shore.

607
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:39,343
He said, “Let's try them.”

608
00:34:42,346 --> 00:34:45,850
In flowering plants,
seeds are covered by protective fruits.

609
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:48,286
While non-flowering plants
produce naked seeds.

610
00:34:48,352 --> 00:34:49,520
Correct!

611
00:34:49,587 --> 00:34:50,955
I PICKED THIS UP
COME, OGOMA

612
00:34:51,022 --> 00:34:51,856
Ogoma.

613
00:34:55,393 --> 00:34:58,096
I need you to help me
with something after school.

614
00:35:00,231 --> 00:35:02,533
I thought I had been caught.

615
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,068
Excuse me.

616
00:35:04,135 --> 00:35:06,404
Ogoma, pick this up.

617
00:35:07,839 --> 00:35:10,575
I thought, "Just say it already."

618
00:35:10,641 --> 00:35:12,844
"Report me if you want!"

619
00:35:14,412 --> 00:35:15,313
Huh?

620
00:35:15,980 --> 00:35:17,248
Bye!

621
00:35:17,315 --> 00:35:18,616
Now that I think about it,

622
00:35:19,183 --> 00:35:23,654
Ms. Aya was stopping me
from crossing a dangerous line.

623
00:35:25,690 --> 00:35:27,558
She never lectured me.

624
00:35:27,625 --> 00:35:29,527
What about the kids who invited you?

625
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:32,029
Were they caught?

626
00:35:37,034 --> 00:35:40,338
Two of them got caught
and were sent to a facility.

627
00:35:41,939 --> 00:35:43,141
One…

628
00:35:45,610 --> 00:35:46,744
Hey, Tetsu!

629
00:35:50,248 --> 00:35:51,315
Hey!

630
00:35:53,951 --> 00:35:55,219
Hey, Tetsu!

631
00:35:55,286 --> 00:35:56,420
Hey!

632
00:36:09,567 --> 00:36:12,203
Hey, Tetsu, please! Wake up!

633
00:36:12,703 --> 00:36:14,605
Please don't die!

634
00:36:15,806 --> 00:36:17,208
Don't die!

635
00:36:18,609 --> 00:36:19,677
Please!

636
00:36:22,813 --> 00:36:24,215
Don't die…

637
00:36:24,282 --> 00:36:25,383
My friend…

638
00:36:26,951 --> 00:36:28,186
died…

639
00:36:29,453 --> 00:36:30,788
in front of me.

640
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:37,995
He was like an older brother to me.

641
00:36:42,333 --> 00:36:46,070
I called an ambulance,
and the police took me in too.

642
00:36:46,137 --> 00:36:48,306
You were doing drugs with him,
weren't you?

643
00:36:48,973 --> 00:36:50,508
I told you I wasn't!

644
00:36:52,610 --> 00:36:53,978
Then why were you there?

645
00:36:54,645 --> 00:36:55,980
I couldn't reach him!

646
00:36:57,715 --> 00:36:59,784
I went to check, that's all.

647
00:36:59,850 --> 00:37:01,252
You did drugs, didn't you?

648
00:37:02,453 --> 00:37:03,321
Admit to it already.

649
00:37:07,959 --> 00:37:11,062
Honestly, I don't care how many idiots
like you end up dying.

650
00:37:11,128 --> 00:37:12,563
Fuck you! I'll kill you!

651
00:37:12,630 --> 00:37:16,000
Go ahead. You're just talk.
Don't underestimate adults.

652
00:37:16,801 --> 00:37:19,837
I'm Ms. Saruwatari
from Koura Middle School.

653
00:37:20,404 --> 00:37:24,942
This boy was helping me
clean the science prep room after school.

654
00:37:25,009 --> 00:37:27,178
It's no use, Teacher.

655
00:37:28,012 --> 00:37:30,248
These kids will grow up to be scum.

656
00:37:30,314 --> 00:37:31,983
Don't just assume that.

657
00:37:34,485 --> 00:37:36,887
There are things
you shouldn't say to a boy

658
00:37:37,622 --> 00:37:40,224
who just lost his friend.

659
00:37:41,926 --> 00:37:42,960
Come on.

660
00:37:50,835 --> 00:37:53,638
We aren't finished interrogating him!

661
00:37:58,843 --> 00:38:02,213
You won't turn into scum. Never.

662
00:38:04,615 --> 00:38:09,887
It was the first time I felt that
an adult was right about something.

663
00:38:11,722 --> 00:38:13,424
I see.

664
00:38:18,462 --> 00:38:19,530
What will you do

665
00:38:20,831 --> 00:38:22,099
if Ms. Aya is the culprit?

666
00:38:25,102 --> 00:38:27,405
If it's true, she'll be arrested.

667
00:38:29,440 --> 00:38:31,442
But if it's a mistake…

668
00:38:35,146 --> 00:38:37,248
I'll repay the kindness

669
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:40,184
she showed me back then.

670
00:38:46,824 --> 00:38:48,826
You already saved her on the mountain.

671
00:38:52,730 --> 00:38:54,265
Not just her.

672
00:38:55,366 --> 00:38:57,068
I want to help everyone I can.

673
00:38:59,203 --> 00:39:00,671
Yes, Ogoma here.

674
00:39:02,473 --> 00:39:03,641
Understood.

675
00:39:08,813 --> 00:39:10,047
I drank the beer.

676
00:39:10,848 --> 00:39:12,650
What is it? Do you need to drive?

677
00:39:12,717 --> 00:39:14,085
-Going somewhere?
-Yes.

678
00:39:14,151 --> 00:39:15,753
Where do you need to go?

679
00:39:15,820 --> 00:39:18,122
Ms. Tabatake has gone missing.

680
00:39:19,056 --> 00:39:20,191
Start with that next time!

681
00:39:22,093 --> 00:39:25,363
She left the hospital
and then went to her apartment.

682
00:39:25,429 --> 00:39:27,064
Let's go there first.

683
00:39:28,632 --> 00:39:29,934
-Put it in.
-Yes.

684
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:31,035
I'll hurry then.

685
00:39:33,337 --> 00:39:34,705
Please do.

686
00:39:47,218 --> 00:39:48,419
Thank you.

687
00:39:52,089 --> 00:39:52,923
Ms. Tabatake!

688
00:39:53,491 --> 00:39:55,126
-Mr. Awashima!
-Ms. Tabatake!

689
00:39:56,327 --> 00:39:57,495
-Get me the key!
-Here!

690
00:39:57,561 --> 00:39:59,130
-Ms. Tabatake!
-Please open it.

691
00:39:59,196 --> 00:40:00,297
It's open!

692
00:40:00,865 --> 00:40:02,199
Ms. Tabatake.

693
00:40:03,267 --> 00:40:05,002
Ms. Tabatake!

694
00:40:05,069 --> 00:40:07,338
Why did she leave the hospital?

695
00:40:23,354 --> 00:40:26,123
Ogoma! Ogoma!

696
00:40:26,190 --> 00:40:27,191
Ogoma!

697
00:40:27,258 --> 00:40:28,659
Why are you here?!

698
00:40:28,726 --> 00:40:30,561
Look up! Ms. Tabatake is on the roof!

699
00:40:32,496 --> 00:40:33,664
Please send backup!

700
00:40:33,731 --> 00:40:34,565
Roger!

701
00:40:44,675 --> 00:40:45,843
Ms. Tabatake.

702
00:40:48,913 --> 00:40:49,914
Are you okay?

703
00:40:49,980 --> 00:40:51,248
Please calm down!

704
00:40:52,950 --> 00:40:53,984
Let's go back to the hospital.

705
00:40:54,618 --> 00:40:55,786
Let's go back!

706
00:40:56,987 --> 00:40:57,922
Okay?

707
00:40:58,989 --> 00:41:00,191
Ms. Tabatake.

708
00:41:00,958 --> 00:41:01,826
Calm down.

709
00:41:01,892 --> 00:41:03,227
It's over!

710
00:41:03,294 --> 00:41:04,495
It's not over!

711
00:41:04,562 --> 00:41:05,396
It's over!

712
00:41:08,065 --> 00:41:09,266
I was so stupid!

713
00:41:09,834 --> 00:41:11,302
I'm also stupid!

714
00:41:13,070 --> 00:41:15,473
If you're in trouble, talk to me.

715
00:41:15,539 --> 00:41:16,841
Let's talk!

716
00:41:16,907 --> 00:41:19,176
We'll listen to your troubles.

717
00:41:22,847 --> 00:41:24,014
Ms. Tabatake!

718
00:41:30,754 --> 00:41:32,389
May I come closer?

719
00:41:36,260 --> 00:41:37,161
Is this okay?

720
00:41:37,761 --> 00:41:38,863
Don't.

721
00:41:40,798 --> 00:41:44,668
What do you call your daughter,
Ms. Tabatake?

722
00:41:46,670 --> 00:41:48,906
Nono?

723
00:41:50,007 --> 00:41:51,542
Or does she have a nickname?

724
00:41:54,945 --> 00:41:55,880
Just Nono.

725
00:41:58,282 --> 00:42:00,150
So you call her Nono.

726
00:42:04,121 --> 00:42:05,089
Nono.

727
00:42:13,797 --> 00:42:14,899
Get her!

728
00:42:17,568 --> 00:42:19,270
Okay.

729
00:42:22,740 --> 00:42:25,509
I'm sorry. Did we hurt you?

730
00:42:27,645 --> 00:42:28,913
Can you stand?

731
00:42:28,979 --> 00:42:30,180
Are you okay?

732
00:42:31,782 --> 00:42:33,317
Let's go back to the hospital.

733
00:42:35,986 --> 00:42:37,354
I can't…

734
00:42:39,123 --> 00:42:40,257
Let's go.

735
00:42:41,292 --> 00:42:42,660
Hello, sir.

736
00:42:51,302 --> 00:42:52,736
Please use Japanese.

737
00:42:53,971 --> 00:42:55,272
Did you get all of that?

738
00:42:55,339 --> 00:42:56,774
I'm checking.

739
00:42:57,942 --> 00:42:59,276
You're okay.

740
00:43:11,922 --> 00:43:12,856
I love you.

741
00:43:18,028 --> 00:43:19,196
It's okay.

742
00:43:21,865 --> 00:43:23,334
I will settle everything.

743
00:43:37,481 --> 00:43:39,683
Ms. Tabatake! Stop!

744
00:43:40,417 --> 00:43:41,719
Ms. Tabatake!

745
00:43:45,489 --> 00:43:46,357
TRANSLATING

746
00:43:46,423 --> 00:43:48,993
They take people to hell.

747
00:44:07,344 --> 00:44:09,880
I have my sister's life insurance policy.

748
00:44:09,947 --> 00:44:12,716
Get a confession from Saruwatari.

749
00:44:12,783 --> 00:44:13,817
What do you think?

750
00:44:13,884 --> 00:44:16,420
Was it really suicide?

751
00:44:16,487 --> 00:44:17,454
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
